From 99313917974976398e519d0cba1514fe189149dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr233 <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:32:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] vgpu: let a launcher name the directory the caches live in

The Vulkan pipeline cache and the metal2vulkan translation cache sit in
$TMPDIR beside the logs. A launcher that gives each virtual machine its
own $TMPDIR therefore gives each machine its own caches, and a machine's
first boot compiles every pipeline again although another machine of
the same guest build already has them. On macOS 26.6.2 one of those
pipelines, CoreAnimation's uber fragment shader, takes NVIDIA's driver
over ten seconds; the guest restarts its GPU about a thousand times
while the submission waits.

REIMS_VGPU_CACHE_DIR, when set and not empty, names the directory both
caches use instead. The logs and the driver breadcrumbs stay in
$TMPDIR. Both caches already publish by rename under per-process
temporary names and check what they read, so machines may share one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
